title: radio_01_adrift
freq: 38.75
left: vulture
right: deer,sterna,bear
name: Call 01 — Adrift
---
vulture: Vulture here.¶Sterna, Bear — status and position.
sterna: Sterna, copy. Outboard passageway, port side.¶Level with the manifold. Tutto tranquillo.
bear: Bear. Three steps behind her, covering the aft ladder.
vulture: Contact?
sterna: Nothing.¶And that's what's strange.
sterna: I swept all three hundred meters of deck with thermal.¶Not one body. Ni uno solo.
bear: And there's no sound inside.
bear: A ship this size always makes noise, boss. Pumps, generators, the hull working.¶The Mariner is silent.
vulture: Listen carefully.¶There is something inside this vessel.
vulture: Move slow and clear every corner.
bear: What about the bridge, boss? Find anything up there?
_beat: pause
vulture: The bridge is compromised.¶Controls destroyed. The ship is adrift.
bear: Great.¶Three hundred meters of tanker with no rudder.
bear: And loaded. That doesn't stop on its own, Vulture.
deer: Compromised how?
deer: Is anyone alive up there, sir?¶What happened?
_beat: silence
vulture: Who said that?
sterna: Bambi.
vulture: Who?
sterna: Deer. The Coast Guard kid.¶The one who's left.
vulture: I forgot about the kid.¶Shit...
vulture: Coast Guard. What happened to your team?
deer: There were five of us.
deer: We came up the starboard side.¶They were on us the second we went in.
deer: Crew. Unarmed.¶We didn't read them as a threat.
deer: They caught us off guard.¶We were overrun before any of us could react.
_beat: silence
deer: It took less than two minutes.¶I'm the only one who walked out.
sterna: Attends.¶Five armed men, against people with no weapons?
deer: Yes.
_beat: silence
deer: They looked hungry.
bear: Boss.¶They sent us out here over a draft that didn't add up.
bear: This isn't crude smuggling.
vulture: No. It isn't.
vulture: Get this straight, all three of you: this stopped being a seizure.
vulture: We're not here to count barrels.¶We're here to find out what is happening on this ship.
sterna: Did you reach Command?
vulture: I tried. Something is jamming long range.¶All we have is this channel.
_beat: silence
vulture: We're on our own, gentlemen.
sterna: Merde.
vulture: I'm going straight down to the lower levels.¶You move along the deck and report anything out of the ordinary.
bear: Copy. We're headed for B Deck.
bear: It's the accommodation block. Most of the berths are there.¶If anyone on this ship is still alive, they're there.
bear: And if the hatches are dogged shut, I'll open them.
deer: Sir. The bridge.¶You didn't answer me whether there was anyone up—
vulture: Bear. Sterna.
vulture: As of now you're his babysitters.¶His safety is on you. Anything happens to him, you answer to me.
bear: We always get the good jobs.
deer: With respect, sir.¶I didn't come here to be looked after.
deer: I won't be dead weight.
bear: I like the kid.¶He's got patriotic spirit.
vulture: Loyalty to a flag isn't worth much in the middle of the ocean, Bear.¶What's worth something is coming back alive.
_beat: pause
vulture: Keep the channel open.¶Vulture out.
===
